  "status": "Refused",
  "description": "Erection of a ground floor rear extension with sukkah roof",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed development, by reason of its poor design, size, bulk, and massing, would result in an obtrusive and incompatible form of development that fails to be subservient to the original dwelling house and fails to respect the architectural integrity of the subject property, the terrace of which it forms part, and the wider area. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D1 (London&#x27;s form, character and capacity for growth), D3 (Optimising site capacity through the design-led approach), D4 (Delivering good design) and D6 (Housing quality and standards) of The London Plan (2021) and policies LP1 (Design Quality and Local Character) and LP17 (Housing Design) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s&amp;nbsp; Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).",
    "The proposal, by reason of its substantial size, bulk, and depth on the boundaries, would have a harmful impact on the amenities of the neighbouring occupiers at No. 22 Mount Pleasant Lane, by way of a loss of light and outlook, and would have an overbearing and tunnelling impact. As such, the proposed development is contrary to policies D6 (Housing quality and standards) of the London Plan (2021), policy LP2 (Development and Amenity) of the Hackney Local Plan 2033 (2020), and the guidance contained within Hackney&#x27;s Residential Extensions and Alterations SPD (2009).&amp;nbsp;"
  ],
